{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"total overtime hours per month for the entire workforce cannot exceed 20 hours per worker,\" do you mean each individual worker can work at most 20 overtime hours in a month (so total overtime is capped at 20 times the number of workers that month), or that the sum of overtime hours across all workers in a month is capped at 20 hours total?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the interpretation of the overtime cap, presenting two mutually exclusive options for one constraint."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the workforce, can the number of workers change from month to month through hiring and firing?",
    "Is the workforce level for a month determined at the start of that month (so workers hired in January are available for January production) — or is there any other timing convention you have in mind?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks two distinct questions: first, whether the workforce size is variable (hiring/firing allowed), and second, the specific timing convention for when workforce changes take effect. A user could answer 'yes' to the first question but still need to specify the timing for the second, or answer 'no' to the first, making the second moot or different. They are semantically independent."
}

